CORE
org.cprover.regression.f12.ModularPackage
--function org.cprover.regression.f12.ModularPackage.caller --modular -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^Invalid function-contract mapping
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
type inconsistency
--
Regression for the JBMC parser bug where Java symbol IDs that
contain '/' (from JVM type descriptors like
`Lorg/cprover/regression/f12/Box;`) were fed to
`parse_function_contract_pair` in
src/goto-instrument/contracts/dynamic-frames/dfcc.cpp,
which split them on '/' and rejected them with
"Invalid function-contract mapping".

The trigger is a JML-/JVerify-annotated method whose
signature includes a reference parameter from a non-default
package. With the bug present, JBMC aborts before
verification with EXIT=6 and the error above. With the fix
in place, modular contract substitution proceeds normally
and verification succeeds.

The Java sources reuse the standard org.strata.jverify.JVerify
shape: `precondition`, `postcondition`, `assigns` are no-op
helper functions JBMC's java_bytecode_contracts pass converts
into JVerify contract clauses.
